1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,800
NEXORA. A hands-on review.

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:07,400
Demo mode lets me sign in without any Firebase keys.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:16,400
I upload a coffee photo. The analyzer describes what's visible, and flags what it can't confirm, like the exact location.

4
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:30,900
Hashtags come in seven groups, each with relevance, competition and a reason. They're labeled AI-estimated, so there are no made-up post counts. I filter for low competition, pick three, and copy them.

5
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:36,900
Captions: five different options, with a character check for each platform.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:47,400
The Post Builder previews each platform, scores the draft out of a hundred, then lets me copy or download. It never posts for you.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,200
Tag suggestions are unverified. You add the real handles yourself.

8
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:57,600
The dashboard shows your own real activity.

9
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:03,300
Verdict: a solid MVP, seven out of ten. Live Gemini quality still needs testing.
